      outcome: 'They run git log to see their commit history. They find the commit hash for "add initial ERC20 implementation" and run git checkout <hash> to restore that version. Every committed snapshot is recoverable. The developer never lost the fee mechanism work — it is in a different commit that they can also return to or merge from. Git\'s history is the safety net for all Cairo Builder labs.',
