      outcome: 'u8 cannot hold this — it maxes at 255. u64 cannot hold this for significant amounts — it runs out around 18 STRK at maximum precision. u256 holds it comfortably and stops the machine if arithmetic would somehow exceed it. felt252 would wrap silently if a crafted input caused overflow. The correct choice: u256. The wrong choice costs money.',
