      outcome: 'Reading view functions never touches the blockchain state — the Starknet node executes the function locally in a read-only context and returns the result. This is why dashboards can poll aggressively. Writing (stake, transfer, approve) creates a real transaction, costs gas, and requires a signed wallet. The SDK distinguishes these: provider.call() for reads, wallet.execute() for writes (next lesson).',
